      <h2 id="faq">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <div class="faq">
        <details open>
          <summary>What is a B2B database?</summary>
          <p class="ans">A B2B database is an organized collection of business contacts and company records, such as names, titles, phone numbers, addresses and industries, used by sales and marketing teams to find and reach prospects.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>How do I choose the best B2B database provider?</summary>
          <p class="ans">Compare accuracy, verification dates, pricing model, delivery format, coverage and compliance guidance. Always request a sample and test it before you commit budget.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Is it safe to buy a B2B email database?</summary>
          <p class="ans">It can be, if you check how recent the emails are, verify them before sending and follow CAN-SPAM rules. Old, unverified lists can bounce heavily and damage your sender reputation.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>What is the difference between a contact database and a leads database?</summary>
